docs/adr/0005-per-task-git-worktrees.md:35:Merge conflicts and integration failures are treated as human attention events. Symphony moves the task to the configured Merge Attention Status, which defaults to `Human attention`, instead of retrying agent work against an integration problem.
docs/adr/0016-protected-path-policy.md:21:Symphony checks for unauthorized protected path changes before Stage Commit. When unauthorized changes are present, Symphony moves the task to the Human Attention Status, keeps the work available for inspection, and does not create the Stage Commit. Because Stage Push follows Stage Commit, Stage Push does not run for that task.
docs/adr/0016-protected-path-policy.md:23:Startup Reconciliation, automated Task Branch Integration, Manual Task Merge, and Batch Pull Request handoff must also respect unresolved protected-path attention. Startup Reconciliation and Manual Task Merge must inspect committed Task Branch work before integration. Batch Pull Request creation remains blocked while protected-path attention is unresolved.
docs/adr/0016-protected-path-policy.md:35:Protected-path attention becomes an operator triage path instead of an agent-retry path because the task requires human scope clarification or human-directed cleanup.
docs/adr/0007-stage-goal-handoff.md:28:Goal Usage is parsed from Codex output only when Codex reports it in a parseable JSON form. Parsed Goal Usage is stored in Runtime State for running, retrying, and attention-needed task details, and is displayed in the Web Dashboard when available.
docs/adr/0017-merge-conflict-resolution-handoff.md:29:True or unresolved conflicts remain visible as human attention, with the Agent Worktree retained.
docs/adr/0009-startup-reconciliation.md:19:Unsafe candidates move to the configured Merge Attention Status and are recorded in Runtime State issue errors. Protected Trunk Branch targets, wrong branches, missing Task Branches, uncommitted Agent Worktree changes, and conflicted integration are attention cases. Startup Reconciliation does not create Stage Commits, does not resolve conflicts, does not rebase, does not force-push, and does not auto-merge into Protected Trunk Branches.
docs/adr/0009-startup-reconciliation.md:21:Runtime State records startup reconciliation diagnostics for merged, already-reconciled, skipped, and attention outcomes. The Terminal Console also prints each outcome during startup.
docs/adr/0009-startup-reconciliation.md:25:Startup recovery is conservative and deterministic. Operators can see what was merged, what was already reconciled, what was ignored because it lacked an Agent Worktree, and what needs manual merge attention. Normal orchestration can continue after the pass, but attention tasks remain paused and non-dispatchable in the same startup session.
